From 19ab500bca50a221f41fb56a5b79b8c94ce05da0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 23:27:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] traffic: Live refresh 200ms -> 100ms matched pair +
 name/MAC/IP identity rows

Owner asked for a faster Live view (10ms). The Live option and the rtrafd
base tick are a matched pair - polling faster than the collector rewrites
live.json only re-reads identical data - so both sides move to 100ms
(owner-approved compromise; 10ms would be ~100 req/s of duplicate frames
against the single-threaded httpd for zero visual gain).

rtrafd.c: TICK_MS 200 -> 100 (heavy cadences unchanged - they are wall-clock
multiples of TPS); live.json dev[] entries now carry the client MAC (cli key,
IP fallback) and top[] entries carry smac resolved from the per-poll ARP
cache (remote dst stays IP-only).

Reaper_Traffic.asp: option value + label 100ms; stored 200ms poll pref
migrated to 100; in-flight XHR guard so a slow response skips ticks instead
of stacking requests; Top Devices (live + history) and Top Talkers rows now
render name (networkmap, same get_clientlist source as the dashboard) with
an ip-and-MAC subline - falls back to raw ip/mac when networkmap has no name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
